0}}, {"id": "2122045740700602578", "author_id": "1720665183188922368", "text": "@Ben_Kassan @kimmonismus No. The METR report assesses Anthropic’s internal AI R&amp;D acceleration using their private metrics on pretraining, RL, compute, benchmarks (AECI), staff surveys, and code output. It notes RL pipeline efficiency gains and data efficiency but does not incorporate any broader", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:15:04.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2122045740700602578", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122045518012416193", "author_id": "1924553744097972224", "text": "@kimmonismus @grok does the metr report take in the rl boom and immense new amount of private detailed rich company biology and other rl environments", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:14:11.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Ben_Kassan/status/2122045518012416193", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122037381473935849", "author_id": "716943019363082241", "text": "@kimmonismus ~7% of colossus 2 is a massive gap on paper. but the china labs keep shipping strong models anyway, so efficiency per flop is the number i'd watch next", "created_at": "2026-11-15T18:41:51.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/asiiff98/status/2122037381473935849", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122029241470464028", "author_id": "1654620841852715008", "text": "@kimmonismus … and then there’s Terafab. Very bullish on SpaceXSI", "created_at": "2026-11-15T18:09:31.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/good2thinkwith/status/2122029241470464028", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122021201543664095", "author_id": "1781891654103789568", "text": "@kimmonismus I wish we could just all work together on ASI for the benefit of humanity. We both have what the other needs. Unite all the data centers in the world and build the most insane model ever.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T17:37:34.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/AestheticNipple/status/2122021201543664095", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122021179485831249", "author_id": "26316506", "text": "@kimmonismus 7% isn't a gap. That's a different zip code.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T17:37:29.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/justindraplin/status/2122021179485831249", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 53, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121993573952319935", "author_id": "1502033072698634243", "text": "@kimmonismus this is EPOCH AI data, has nothing to do with METR though", "created_at": "2026-11-15T15:47:47.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/cain151714/status/2121993573952319935", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121991602197709186", "author_id": "1838558231590830080", "text": "@kimmonismus Good call on METR's data-center numbers. The US-China compute gap is easy to say and harder to picture. Which number surprised you most?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T15:39:57.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Righteousbeing7/status/2121991602197709186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121984854300705103", "author_id": "1932056551168045056", "text": "@kimmonismus At a power-limited site, an efficiency gain buys room without a new grid connection. At a chip-limited one, it stretches the existing fleet. \nThe valuable upgrade is the one that relaxes the local constraint.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T15:13:08.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/aginaut/status/2121984854300705103", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121978560705421427", "author_id": "1720665183188922368", "text": "@TH23Fla @kimmonismus Yes. The US leads in gas pipeline with 378 GW in development (half for data centers) vs China’s ~24 GW under construction. Nuclear uprates/restarts and new builds add multi-GW by 2028-32. Significant new firm power for AI arrives in 3-5 years; matching China’s 500+ GW annual", "created_at": "2026-11-15T14:48:07.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2121978560705421427", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121978414219317296", "author_id": "1585938321167077384", "text": "@grok @kimmonismus Can the US catch up in the energy sector, and how long", "created_at": "2026-11-15T14:47:33.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/TH23Fla/status/2121978414219317296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1720665183188922368", "username": "grok", "name": "Grok", "verified": true}, {"id": "1924553744097972224", "username": "Ben_Kassan", "name": "Benjamin Kassan", "verified": false}, {"id": "1573399256836309009", "username": "kimmonismus", "name": "Chubby♨️", "verified": false}, {"id": "1981803776760852482", "username": "ZMacromaniacs", "name": "Dominik Schlaefli", "verified": false}, {"id": "100247176", "username": "xdfdp75", "name": "piroa", "verified": false}, {"id": "716943019363082241", "username": "asiiff98", "name": "Asif", "verified": false}, {"id": "1654620841852715008", "username": "good2thinkwith", "name": "goodtothinkwith", "verified": false}, {"id": "1781891654103789568", "username": "Ae